            "accordion_row_GpGfEt": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "HOW SHOULD I CARE FOR MY LEATHER PRODUCT TO ENSURE IT LASTS A LONG TIME?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "leather",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_xkKGPc": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "name": "t:names.text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>TO MAINTAIN THE BEAUTY AND LONGEVITY OF YOUR LEATHER GOODS, WE RECOMMEND THE FOLLOWING CARE TIPS:REGULAR CLEANING: WIPE YOUR LEATHER PRODUCT WITH A SOFT, DRY CLOTH TO REMOVE DUST AND DIRT. AVOID USING WATER OR SOAP, AS THESE CAN DAMAGE THE LEATHER.CONDITIONING: USE A HIGH-QUALITY LEATHER CONDITIONER EVERY 6-12 MONTHS TO KEEP THE LEATHER SOFT AND PREVENT IT FROM DRYING OUT OR CRACKING. APPLY THE CONDITIONER WITH A SOFT CLOTH, FOLLOWING THE PRODUCT INSTRUCTIONS.STORAGE: STORE YOUR LEATHER ITEMS IN A COOL, DRY PLACE AWAY FROM DIRECT SUNLIGHT, WHICH CAN CAUSE THE COLOR TO FADE. USE A DUST BAG OR PILLOWCASE TO PROTECT THE LEATHER FROM DUST AND SCRATCHES.AVOID MOISTURE: KEEP YOUR LEATHER GOODS AWAY FROM WATER. IF THEY DO GET WET, BLOT THE EXCESS WATER WITH A DRY CLOTH AND ALLOW THEM TO AIR DRY NATURALLY, AWAY FROM HEAT SOURCES.HANDLING: WHEN HANDLING LEATHER PRODUCTS, MAKE SURE YOUR HANDS ARE CLEAN AND DRY. OILS AND DIRT FROM YOUR HANDS CAN STAIN THE LEATHER OVER TIME.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "alignment": "left",
